# Advisory notification formats

Customers do **not** share a message format. Each one has its own approved
wording, stored per customer and edited on the Customers page, so onboarding a
client is configuration rather than a code change.

Storage: `customers.notification_template` and `customers.ti_notification_template`,
with `customers.slack_channels` holding the destinations. The templates below
are the seeds in `EmergingJoes/advisory_notification.py`; once a customer row
exists, the **database is the source of truth**, not the constant.

## Evoke — structured field block

`NOTIFICATION_TEMPLATE` / `EVOKE_VULN_TEMPLATE`. Do not reword the labels,
reorder the fields, or add sections.

```
Security Vulnerability Notification

Advisory Date: [DD Month YYYY]
Vulnerability Name: [Vulnerability or advisory name]
Vendor / Product: [Vendor and affected product]
CVE(s): [CVE ID(s)]
Advisory ID: [Vendor advisory ID / N/A]
Severity: [Critical / High / Medium / Low]
Affected Versions: [Affected version(s)]
Fixed Version: [Fixed version / Not available]

Description:
[Briefly describe the vulnerability, exploitation requirements, and potential impact.]

Recommendations:
• [Required patch, upgrade, mitigation, or validation action]
• [Priority and requested completion date]
Attachments:
• [Advisory filename].pdf — Security advisory
```

Note there is no blank line between the last recommendation bullet and `Attachments:`.

Threat intelligence variant (`kind = 'threat_intelligence'`): same layout,
retitled `Threat Intelligence Notification`, `Vulnerability Name` reads
`Threat Name`, and the `CVE(s)`, `Affected Versions` and `Fixed Version` lines
are removed. Everything else, including `Advisory ID` and the priority bullet,
is unchanged.

## Fidelidade — covering note

`FIDELIDADE_VULN_TEMPLATE`. Prose, not a field block. The literal
`@SOCIberia_DXC` mention and the `[Security Advisory]` tag line are part of the
approved format and must survive rendering verbatim.

```
Hello,

We are sharing the attached advisory regarding <CVE-ID> (<VULNERABILITY-NAME>), a <VULNERABILITY-TYPE / SHORT DESCRIPTION> affecting <AFFECTED PRODUCT / COMPONENT> that <BRIEF DESCRIPTION OF HOW THE VULNERABILITY CAN BE TRIGGERED OR EXPLOITED>.

Please review the attached advisory, validating <WHAT SHOULD BE CHECKED / EXPOSURE CONDITION>, and prioritizing <PATCHING / MITIGATION ACTION> for <SYSTEMS OR ASSETS THAT SHOULD RECEIVE PRIORITY>.

[Security Advisory] @SOCIberia_DXC [<SEVERITY>]

Thanks,
```

The threat intelligence variant (`FIDELIDADE_TI_TEMPLATE`) was derived from the
above, since TI advisories carry no CVE or version numbers. It has **not** been
confirmed by the business — check before relying on it.

## Implementation rules

- Templates are Slack mrkdwn emitted **verbatim**. Only substituted values are
  escaped, so mentions, tag lines and bold markers survive.
- Placeholders are `<UPPERCASE>` tokens, matched by `PLACEHOLDER_RE`. Lowercase
  text in angle brackets is left alone so ordinary prose is never eaten.
- The LLM returns **field values as JSON only**. Layout is substituted in code by
  `render_template()` and `render()`, both of which must stay pure (no network,
  config, or file reads) so message shape is testable without an API key.
- Never let the model emit the assembled message; it drops and renames lines.
- Tokens in `COMPUTED_TOKENS` are filled from data we already hold and are never
  sent to the model. Advisory Date, Attachments, CVE, severity and the priority
  bullet are all computed. Remediation deadlines come from `REMEDIATION_DAYS`.
- Unknown fields render as `N/A` (or `Not available` for Fixed Version). The
  prompt forbids guessing versions, advisory IDs, and severities.
- Message building must never block distribution: fall back to database-derived
  fields on any failure, and to the standard field block when a customer has no
  template.
- Changing a seed constant does **not** change an existing customer. Backfill
  only fills columns that are still empty, so an analyst's edit always wins.
- Do **not** put the cross-article "which other customers are affected" roll-up
  into the message. Even with per-customer channels, it would leak one client's
  exposure to another.
